Package: aapalette
Title: Amino-Acid Colour Palettes for Sequence Visualisation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("AApalette", "Project", , "slj38@cam.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A curated set of amino-acid colour palettes for protein sequence
    figures. Provides three new palettes from the AApalette project ('hue' for
    normal vision, 'redgreen' for red-green colour-vision deficiency, and
    'tritan' for tritanopia) alongside seven attributed community-standard
    schemes ('clustal', 'zappo', 'taylor', 'lesk', 'cinema', 'rasmol',
    'shapely'). All colours are loaded from a single bundled JSON source of
    truth so that the R, Python and Jalview siblings stay consistent. Includes
    'ggplot2' colour and fill scales keyed on residue letters and base-graphics
    swatch helpers.
